WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.403 --> 00:00:02.820
STEPHANIE WONG:
Hi, I'm Stephanie.

00:00:02.820 --> 00:00:05.700
And today we're going to look
at how you can build a real time

00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:09.630
inventory management system
using Google Cloud Spanner.

00:00:09.630 --> 00:00:12.810
Consumers are more digitally
connected than ever before.

00:00:12.810 --> 00:00:15.240
Expectations for omnichannel
shopping experiences

00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:18.270
across online and offline
channels have increased.

00:00:18.270 --> 00:00:20.730
Experiences like buy
online, pickup in store

00:00:20.730 --> 00:00:24.030
are expected now, rather than
considered a convenience.

00:00:24.030 --> 00:00:27.080
For a company like Maxim
Modish, a fictional retailer,

00:00:27.080 --> 00:00:29.850
in-person shopping has been the
backbone of their retail model

00:00:29.850 --> 00:00:30.900
for years.

00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:33.630
As a premier retailer, they have
hundreds of department stores

00:00:33.630 --> 00:00:34.920
across the nation.

00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:36.930
But to meet increasing
online demands,

00:00:36.930 --> 00:00:39.840
they've had to undergo a
digital transformation.

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:41.970
In recent years,
Maxim Modish customers

00:00:41.970 --> 00:00:44.340
have been engaging with them
through multiple channels,

00:00:44.340 --> 00:00:48.310
online through social
media, in-store, and in app.

00:00:48.310 --> 00:00:51.210
Naturally, these customers
expect a seamless experience

00:00:51.210 --> 00:00:52.950
across all of these channels.

00:00:52.950 --> 00:00:54.660
To better meet
these expectations,

00:00:54.660 --> 00:00:57.780
Maxim Modish needed a complete
picture of their inventory flow

00:00:57.780 --> 00:01:00.340
and real time decision
making at scale.

00:01:00.340 --> 00:01:01.860
This revealed three
key challenges

00:01:01.860 --> 00:01:04.290
they faced with their
technology stack.

00:01:04.290 --> 00:01:07.350
One, inconsistent view
of data across silos.

00:01:07.350 --> 00:01:10.140
Two, cost inefficiencies
to management overhead

00:01:10.140 --> 00:01:11.700
and seasonal scaling needs.

00:01:11.700 --> 00:01:15.550
Three, an inability to evolve
with new business needs.

00:01:15.550 --> 00:01:17.190
This was a tough
problem to solve.

00:01:17.190 --> 00:01:19.650
They were dealing with an
extremely large amount of data

00:01:19.650 --> 00:01:22.020
requiring them to integrate
event data from hundreds

00:01:22.020 --> 00:01:24.750
of siloed data sources
in a timely manner.

00:01:24.750 --> 00:01:27.000
These inventory events
were coming in rapidly

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:28.740
and constantly
changing, resulting

00:01:28.740 --> 00:01:30.300
in a lack of
real-time consistency

00:01:30.300 --> 00:01:32.080
across data sources.

00:01:32.080 --> 00:01:34.590
For example, a woman's
dress would show in stock

00:01:34.590 --> 00:01:37.100
on the mobile shopping app,
but the same dress showed out

00:01:37.100 --> 00:01:39.780
of stock in the physical store.

00:01:39.780 --> 00:01:41.490
Additionally, running
their existing

00:01:41.490 --> 00:01:44.840
on-premise infrastructure led
to numerous cost inefficiencies.

00:01:44.840 --> 00:01:46.590
To keep up with the
growing volume of data

00:01:46.590 --> 00:01:49.530
and meet seasonal scaling
during times like black Friday,

00:01:49.530 --> 00:01:51.630
they had to increase
their on-prem data center

00:01:51.630 --> 00:01:55.110
for peak capacity, which
aggravated operational costs

00:01:55.110 --> 00:01:58.260
and tied up resources
managing that infrastructure.

00:01:58.260 --> 00:02:01.560
Last, they were unable to
evolve with new business needs.

00:02:01.560 --> 00:02:03.270
Running antiquated
systems, it was

00:02:03.270 --> 00:02:06.300
difficult to adapt or
modernize their applications.

00:02:06.300 --> 00:02:08.190
Applying changes to
monolithic systems

00:02:08.190 --> 00:02:10.270
is a long, arduous process.

00:02:10.270 --> 00:02:13.230
This is where Google Cloud
helped turn things around.

00:02:13.230 --> 00:02:15.090
Through their
partnership, Maxim Modish

00:02:15.090 --> 00:02:18.060
was able to build an inventory
ledger solution with Google

00:02:18.060 --> 00:02:20.050
Cloud Spanner at its core.

00:02:20.050 --> 00:02:21.750
This inventory
ledger solution is

00:02:21.750 --> 00:02:24.090
modeled based on retail
environments represented

00:02:24.090 --> 00:02:25.930
as a series of events.

00:02:25.930 --> 00:02:27.540
These events include
things like items

00:02:27.540 --> 00:02:30.960
shipped to a store, item price
updates, or customer purchase

00:02:30.960 --> 00:02:31.950
requests.

00:02:31.950 --> 00:02:34.050
They chose Spanner to
house their inventory event

00:02:34.050 --> 00:02:36.510
ledger, which would keep
track of the constant changes

00:02:36.510 --> 00:02:37.860
to inventory.

00:02:37.860 --> 00:02:39.780
Cloud Spanner is
a managed database

00:02:39.780 --> 00:02:42.840
with strong consistency in
regional and multi-regional

00:02:42.840 --> 00:02:46.560
setup, no downtime,
and scale insurance.

00:02:46.560 --> 00:02:49.770
It combines the best of
relational semantics and scale.

00:02:49.770 --> 00:02:52.120
In addition, Spanner
is a managed service,

00:02:52.120 --> 00:02:54.750
which frees Maxim Modish
from operational overhead

00:02:54.750 --> 00:02:57.810
of their own large
scale inventory systems.

00:02:57.810 --> 00:02:59.950
Whenever an inventory
event happens,

00:02:59.950 --> 00:03:03.420
it's placed in an append-only
immutable event ledger.

00:03:03.420 --> 00:03:05.310
This guarantees
inventory changes

00:03:05.310 --> 00:03:07.530
are recorded in the
system consistently

00:03:07.530 --> 00:03:09.660
across multiple regions.

00:03:09.660 --> 00:03:12.060
As customers buy items
across different channels,

00:03:12.060 --> 00:03:15.060
in-store or mobile, Spanner
gives them a consistent view

00:03:15.060 --> 00:03:17.910
of the inventory no matter what
region or channel the shopper

00:03:17.910 --> 00:03:18.990
comes from.

00:03:18.990 --> 00:03:20.760
All replicas of the
inventory ledger

00:03:20.760 --> 00:03:23.850
are kept up to date, in-sync,
and quickly available.

00:03:23.850 --> 00:03:25.680
What's more, data
housed in Spanner

00:03:25.680 --> 00:03:28.980
is easily available to other
Google Cloud Services, making

00:03:28.980 --> 00:03:31.530
it simple for Maxim Modish
to leverage capabilities

00:03:31.530 --> 00:03:34.500
like BigQuery for
SQL base analytics,

00:03:34.500 --> 00:03:36.270
Looker for modeling
and reporting,

00:03:36.270 --> 00:03:38.580
and AutoML and
BigQuery ML to apply

00:03:38.580 --> 00:03:41.530
machine learning for smarter
real-time decision making.

00:03:41.530 --> 00:03:43.830
For example, Maxim Modish
is able to integrate

00:03:43.830 --> 00:03:46.290
BigQuery to create
this Looker dashboard.

00:03:46.290 --> 00:03:47.790
They can conduct
further analysis

00:03:47.790 --> 00:03:50.520
using BigQuery as a managed
data warehouse and Looker

00:03:50.520 --> 00:03:53.700
for interactive visualizations
across all stores.

00:03:53.700 --> 00:03:55.860
By implementing this
inventory ledger solution

00:03:55.860 --> 00:03:57.900
with Cloud Spanner,
Maxim Modish now

00:03:57.900 --> 00:04:01.290
has real-time view of inventory
across hundreds of data sources

00:04:01.290 --> 00:04:04.440
and applications, the
ability to scale up and down

00:04:04.440 --> 00:04:07.470
to support peak traffic
during large shopping events,

00:04:07.470 --> 00:04:10.410
manage services which
significantly decreases burdens

00:04:10.410 --> 00:04:13.170
of operations, and the
ability to modernize

00:04:13.170 --> 00:04:15.840
and adapt to new business
needs through an ecosystem

00:04:15.840 --> 00:04:17.910
of integrated cloud services.

00:04:17.910 --> 00:04:20.430
By leveraging just some of the
powerful features of Google

00:04:20.430 --> 00:04:24.030
Cloud, Maxim Modish is now able
to do real-time decision making

00:04:24.030 --> 00:04:27.630
for omnichannel retail and build
a seamless online and offline

00:04:27.630 --> 00:04:30.480
shopping experience for
thousands of happy customers

00:04:30.480 --> 00:04:32.303
using a single source of truth.

00:04:32.303 --> 00:04:34.470
Check out the link here to
learn more about Spanner.

00:04:34.470 --> 00:04:39.020
[MUSIC PLAYING]

